version: "2.0"
description: >-
  Warpline Guard — the GitHub Action packaging of the Warpline oracle (P3 Lane
  B, roadmap-2026H2). On pull_request it runs #oracle on PR-head × base (the
  engine computes the merge-base), applies the KNOT-SIZE THRESHOLD (default 6 —
  the 50%-churn-validated stratum from the 18-hit ground truth; ≥10-symbol flag
  sets were 0% and are folded, never listed), and renders the verdict as a job
  summary + JSON report + step outputs. ADVISORY BY DEFAULT: fail-on-flag is
  false, so the check reports and never blocks; with fail-on-flag true it fails
  on in-stratum flags AND fails closed on engine errors. Read-only forever: the
  oracle runs with noWrite, nothing is written to the adjudicated repo except
  the report file. Consumes @a-company/warpline exported functions only — never
  vendors or edits engine code. private:true, unpublished (npm AND Marketplace;
  the founder publishes).

components:
  guard-report:
    description: >-
      src/report.ts — the pure diff-of-verdicts core: OracleRecord →
      GuardReport. Verdict ladder (git-conflict > clean > ripple-only > flagged
      > avalanche), the knot-size threshold over the oracle's RAW knotSize (the
      validated ranking key), the paths filter (minimal glob: **, *, ?) that
      narrows listing/failure but never the stratum, per-flag detail (kind,
      conflicting slots, dangle target, BOTH branches' touch points from the
      justifications), and the honest SCOPE_LINE rendered on every report. No
      I/O — fully unit-tested.
  guard-render:
    description: >-
      src/render.ts — GuardReport → GitHub job-summary markdown + terse log
      lines. Wording discipline (TD-2026-07-16-810) is enforced by test: scoped
      claims only, ripple always folded to a count, avalanche never lists
      symbols, scope line on every render, banned-phrase regex sweep in
      test/render.test.ts.
  guard-main:
    description: >-
      src/main.ts — the composite-action entrypoint (node dist/main.js). Env →
      inputs, base/head resolution from the pull_request event payload when
      inputs are empty, oracle run (noWrite), report JSON + GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY
      + GITHUB_OUTPUT, exit policy: verdicts never fail unless fail-on-flag;
      engine errors fail only when enforcing (fail closed); config errors
      always fail. Action-runner code — stdout is the Actions convention,
      confined to this file.
  guard-action-packaging:
    description: >-
      action.yml (composite, node20 runtime via the caller's setup-node) +
      .github/workflows/warpline-guard.yml (the repo self-test: advisory,
      continue-on-error, fail-on-flag false). test/action-packaging.test.ts is
      the packaging lint: YAML validity, every input threaded to
      WARPLINE_INPUT_* env, outputs wired to the guard step, safe defaults, no
      expression smuggled into input defaults, self-test stays non-blocking.
